# Graphify per-machine manifest
graphify-out/manifest.json

# Vendored libduckdb-sys workaround for upstream duckdb-rs#786.
# Populated by scripts/vendor-duckdb-rs.sh + patches/duckdb-rs-msvc-1940.patch
# Tracked OUT of source control because the script reproduces it deterministically.
# Remove this entry when the upstream patch ships in a released duckdb crate.
vendor/*
# EXCEPT the two manifest-only stub paths inside the duckdb-rs vendor:
# Dependabot's `cargo metadata` and `cargo update` both walk
# `[patch.crates-io] libduckdb-sys = { path = "vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/
# libduckdb-sys" }` from the workspace manifest. With vendor/ fully ignored,
# that path doesn't exist in Dependabot's container (which doesn't run our
# vendor script) and the resolver bails with
# `dependency_file_not_resolvable: failed to read .../Cargo.toml`, failing
# the weekly Dependabot Cargo job on any update that triggers a workspace
# resolve.
#
# Committing JUST the manifest + a stub `src/lib.rs` (byte-identical to what
# `scripts/vendor-duckdb-rs.sh` produces — verified across two fresh runs)
# lets the resolver succeed without committing the full 19 MB vendored
# tree. The script's `rm -rf` + re-vendor pass overwrites these with the
# same bytes, so `git status` stays clean after CI / local builds.
#
# Gitignore pitfall: git's docs say "It is not possible to re-include a
# file if a parent directory of that file is excluded." The classic
# `vendor/` form excludes the directory itself, blocking recursion. Using
# `vendor/*` excludes only the dir's contents (one level), keeping the
# parent walkable so the negations below can re-include specific files.
# Each intermediate directory on the path to the target files must be
# explicitly un-ignored or git won't descend into them either.
!vendor/duckdb-rs
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/Cargo.toml
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/src
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/src/lib.rs
# Re-ignore everything else inside the un-ignored directories so only the
# two leaf paths above are trackable.
vendor/duckdb-rs/*
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates
vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/*
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys
vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/*
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/Cargo.toml
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/src
vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/src/*
!vendor/duckdb-rs/crates/libduckdb-sys/src/lib.rs

# Session-tooling artefacts — runtime state generated per developer
# by Claude Code / devt / graphify / serena / per-project MCP servers.
# Catches everything the narrow rules above didn't, after a v0.5.x
# session accidentally committed ~480k lines of these files into
# branches twice in one sitting. The narrow rules above stay for
# back-compat but are now no-ops under these broader catch-alls.
.claude/
.devt/
.serena/
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.md

# Graphify pipeline outputs — graphs, manifests, cost reports,
# semantic labels. All regenerable from source via `graphify build`;
# no value in tracking them and each graph.json is 100k+ lines.
graphify-out/
